**1. POSITION VACANT: Senior Leadership Role – Manufacturing & Industrial Competitiveness, New Delhi**

**2. ORGANISATION OVERVIEW:**

The organisation is a leading national institution in India’s industry and policy ecosystem, working at the intersection of business, public policy, knowledge and capability development. It works closely with business leaders, Government, academia, research institutions and international partners to promote industrial growth, competitiveness, innovation and sustainable economic development. With a long-standing presence in India’s economic and industrial landscape, the organisation contributes to shaping policy, strengthening industry capabilities and facilitating platforms for collaboration and knowledge exchange.

Within this broader mandate, the organisation’s manufacturing portfolio spans established and emerging sectors, with a focus on productivity and competitiveness, technology adoption, supply-chain resilience, exports, sustainability, research, knowledge exchange and industry capability development.

**3. JOB DESCRIPTION/ RESPONSIBILITIES:**

The senior leader will provide strategic leadership to a major national manufacturing portfolio, helping Indian manufacturing enterprises address the challenges and opportunities affecting competitiveness and growth. The role requires a grounded understanding of manufacturing sectors and the ability to translate industry needs into practical interventions across policy, technology absorption, productivity, capability development and international competitiveness.

The ideal candidate will be a grounded, highly credible manufacturing leader who understands industry from the inside, is trusted by senior business leaders, can engage Government constructively, and can convert sector challenges into practical solutions. The role also offers the opportunity to build and lead an overarching manufacturing knowledge, innovation and capability platform, with specialist or thematic initiatives developed in response to evolving industry priorities.

**Key Responsibilities:**

**(A) Manufacturing Competitiveness & Industry Transformation:**

(1) Maintain a close understanding of the operating, policy, technology and market challenges facing manufacturing enterprises and use these insights to shape the organisation’s priorities and interventions;

(2) Design sector-specific initiatives to strengthen competitiveness, productivity, domestic value addition, supply-chain resilience and export performance;

(3) Accelerate industry awareness, evaluation and absorption of lean and quality systems, digital transformation, Industry 4.0, advanced manufacturing technologies, sustainable practices and other productivity-enhancing innovations;

(4) Support enterprises in accessing international markets, integrating into global value chains and learning from leading manufacturing ecosystems, while helping them navigate evolving standards, regulation and compliance.

**(B) Policy Engagement & Government Advisory:**

(1) Set and lead the manufacturing policy agenda, with a focus on competitiveness, productivity, global integration, supply-chain resilience, trade, tariffs, logistics, standards, sustainability and technology adoption;

(2) Engage at senior levels with Union Ministries, Government institutions, regulators and policy bodies on manufacturing-related priorities, regulatory issues and structural constraints;

(3) Lead preparation of evidence-based policy recommendations, position papers, consultation responses and policy inputs to Government, grounded in research and stakeholder perspectives;

(4) Anchor high-level dialogue between industry and Government, including consultations and task forces, and ensure effective follow-through on priority issues.

**(C) Manufacturing Knowledge, Innovation & Capability Platforms:**

(1) Lead the development and strategic direction of an overarching manufacturing platform dedicated to knowledge, innovation and capability-building, with flexibility to develop specialist or thematic initiatives under it based on emerging industry priorities;

(2) Define the platform’s strategic focus, programme architecture, operating model, team and expert network, and position it as an authoritative national vehicle for manufacturing knowledge, capability and transformation;

(3) Curate and disseminate national and international best practices, benchmarking, global learning, emerging technologies, innovations and new business and operating models relevant to Indian manufacturing;

(4) Build partnerships with leading companies, technology providers, research institutions, academia and international centres of expertise to bring cutting-edge knowledge and solutions to industry;

(5) Translate knowledge into action on the ground through pilots, capability-building, advisory initiatives, benchmarking, standards and other scalable interventions;

(6) Build a sustainable portfolio of programmes, partnerships and revenue streams that secures the long-term institutional and financial viability of the platform and its initiatives.

**(D) Research, Insight & Thought Leadership:**

(1) Lead the manufacturing research and knowledge agenda, including sector studies, surveys, policy briefs, white papers and analyses on industry trends, global value chains and competitiveness;

(2) Develop thought leadership on smart and advanced manufacturing, digitalisation, green manufacturing, circular economy, resilient supply chains and other emerging themes;

(3) Build research and knowledge partnerships with think tanks, academic institutions, technology organisations and international institutions;

(4) Position the organisation as an authoritative national voice on manufacturing competitiveness and transformation.

**(E) Industry Convening & Strategic Partnerships:**

(1) Conceptualise and lead flagship national and international convenings on manufacturing, including leadership forums, conferences, summits and roundtables, and curate their agendas with business and Government leaders;

(2) Ensure high-quality programme management and execution of large-scale engagements, including coordination with stakeholders, speakers and partners;

(3) Build strong, trusted relationships with business leaders across large enterprises, MSMEs, emerging technology firms and relevant sector associations;

(4) Facilitate structured consultations that convert sector perspectives into actionable policy, programme and knowledge priorities;

(5) Build strategic partnerships with national and international institutions that strengthen the manufacturing agenda and deepen the value delivered to industry stakeholders.

**(F) Team Leadership & Portfolio Delivery:**

(1) Steer senior industry advisory groups, expert forums and strategic initiatives with clear priorities, accountabilities and outcomes;

(2) Guide internal teams in executing research, policy engagement, industry programmes, publications, consultations and events, ensuring timely and high-quality delivery;

(3) Build, lead and develop a high-performing, multi-disciplinary team with strong sector capability, accountability and execution discipline;

(4) Strengthen the organisation’s institutional engagement with industry, Government and national/international partners.

**(G) Financial Leadership & Resource Mobilisation:**

(1) Share accountability with senior leadership for the financial performance and P&L of the manufacturing portfolio;

(2) Develop and implement an annual revenue and resource-mobilisation plan with clear revenue streams, targets, timelines and accountabilities;

(3) Build a diversified pipeline of programmes, projects, partnerships and knowledge initiatives that provides predictable, multi-year revenue visibility;

(4) Prepare business cases, budgets, pricing/revenue models and financial projections for significant new initiatives, and oversee contribution margins, receivables, cost discipline and efficient use of resources;

(5) Monitor financial performance closely, identify potential shortfalls early and initiate timely corrective action;

(6) Balance financial sustainability with the quality, independence and credibility of policy, research and stakeholder-facing work.

**4. QUALIFICATIONS, EXPERIENCE AND COMPETENCIES:**

**Qualifications:**

Master’s degree in Engineering, Manufacturing, Industrial Management, Economics, Public Policy or a related discipline from a reputed institution.

**Experience:**

(1) Minimum 20+ years of professional experience in manufacturing, industrial policy, industry development or related domains, with substantial senior leadership responsibility;

(2) Senior leadership experience in industry, consulting, policy or knowledge institutions, or comparable organisations will be preferred;

(3) Demonstrated depth of engagement with operating businesses and strong understanding of the commercial, technological, regulatory and competitive challenges confronting manufacturing enterprises;

(4) Proven experience engaging senior Government stakeholders, industry leaders and multi-stakeholder platforms;

(5) Demonstrated ability to lead high-impact programmes, research/knowledge initiatives, industry platforms and large teams;

(6) Experience building or scaling an institutional platform, business unit, centre, practice or comparable initiative will be strongly valued, particularly where it involved technology/innovation, knowledge partnerships and financial sustainability.

**Skills and Competencies:**

(1) Grounded sector judgement, strategic thinking, policy analysis and broad manufacturing perspective;

(2) Government, regulatory and industry engagement;

(3) CEO-level stakeholder management, convening and relationship building;

(4) Thought leadership, research and knowledge development;

(5) Institution building, technology/innovation orientation and global perspective;

(6) Business development, financial acumen and resource mobilisation;

(7) Strategic communication, influencing and public speaking;

(8) Team leadership, development and performance management;

(9) Collaboration, partnership building and execution orientation.

**5. COMPENSATION OFFERED:**

Annual salary for the role is attractive and aligned to market rates. The offer made to the selected candidate will be commensurate with qualifications, experience, and salary history.

**6. LOCATION: New Delhi**

The role will involve regular travel, as required for industry engagement, stakeholder interactions and key programmes and initiatives.

**7. REFERENCE: SL-MFG-CONF**

**8. CONTACT INFORMATION:**

Team SAMS

Strategic Alliance Management Services P Ltd.

1/1B, Choudhary Hetram House, Bharat Nagar

New Friends Colony, New Delhi 110 025

Phone Nos.: 011-4081 9900; 4165 3612

**9. APPLICATION PROCESS:**

Eligible candidates interested in the position are requested to apply through the SAMS recruitment platform using the link below by or before October 31, 226. All applications and enquiries will be handled on a strictly confidential basis. The precise designation and identity of the hiring institution will be disclosed to selected candidates at an appropriate stage of the process.

